  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q37-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "37",
    "prompt": "Let $ax^2+bx+c=0$ have roots $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find the following in terms of $a$, $b$ and $c$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p43-q37-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^2+\\beta^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{b^2-2ac}{a^2}$",
          "worked": "Using $\\alpha+\\beta=-\\dfrac ba$ and $\\alpha\\beta=\\dfrac ca$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=(\\alpha+\\beta)^2-2\\alpha\\beta\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=\\left(-\\frac ba\\right)^2-2\\left(\\frac ca\\right)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2&=\\frac{b^2-2ac}{a^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q37-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha\\beta^2+\\alpha^2\\beta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{bc}{a^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha\\beta^2+\\alpha^2\\beta&=\\alpha\\beta(\\alpha+\\beta)\\\\\\alpha\\beta^2+\\alpha^2\\beta&=\\frac ca\\left(-\\frac ba\\right)\\\\\\alpha\\beta^2+\\alpha^2\\beta&=-\\frac{bc}{a^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q37-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac bc$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta&=\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta}\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta&=\\frac{-b/a}{c/a}\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta&=-\\frac bc.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-q37-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1{\\alpha^2}+\\dfrac1{\\beta^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{b^2-2ac}{c^2}$",
          "worked": "Use the sum of squares from part (a).\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\alpha^2}+\\frac1{\\beta^2}&=\\frac{\\alpha^2+\\beta^2}{(\\alpha\\beta)^2}\\\\\\frac1{\\alpha^2}+\\frac1{\\beta^2}&=\\frac{(b^2-2ac)/a^2}{(c/a)^2}\\\\\\frac1{\\alpha^2}+\\frac1{\\beta^2}&=\\frac{b^2-2ac}{c^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
